# Dev-only config
.vscode/
.github/

# Every env file, matching .gitignore. `.env*.local` alone left a plain `.env`
# or a local `.env.production` — the files that hold STRIPE_SECRET_KEY and
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET — free to ride along in the upload a CLI
# `vercel deploy` makes from this working tree. Env vars belong in the Vercel
# project, never in the deployment payload.
.env
.env*
!.env.example

# Docs (not needed at runtime)
*.md
!README.md
